---
import BlogsLayout from '../../../layouts/blogslayout.astro';
---
<BlogsLayout title="Windows 365 Enterprise Deployment Guide" description="A complete architecture framework for setting up, provisioning, and securing Windows 365 Cloud PCs at scale.">
  <header class="article-header">
    <h1>Windows 365 Enterprise Deployment Guide</h1>
    <p class="dek">Standardize cloud virtual desktop delivery across remote workforces with customized provisioning policies and strict baseline compliance.</p>
    <p class="meta">By Akash Nagapure · August 2026 · 6 min read</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Network Connectivity & Azure Network Connections</h2>
    <p>Establish secure hybrid connectivity using Azure Network Connections (ANC) or Microsoft Entra hybrid join criteria depending on your legacy line-of-business app dependencies.</p>
    <h2>Provisioning Policies</h2>
    <p>Assign specific image types (such as Windows 11 Enterprise with Microsoft 365 Apps pre-installed) to dedicated user groups based on operational job roles.</p>
  </div>
</BlogsLayout>
<style>
  .article-header h1 { color:#fff; font-size:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,5.5rem); line-height:1; max-width:12ch; margin:1rem 0; }
  .dek { font-size:1.15rem; line-height:1.7; max-width:42rem; }
  .meta { color:#38bdf8; font:.75rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; }
  .prose { max-width:42rem; font-size:1.05rem; line-height:1.8; margin-top:2rem; }
  .prose h2 { color:#fff; margin-top:2.5rem; }
</style>